{%- comment -%}
  This file sits at the repository root, not in _pages/ beside its Italian twin,
  and the asymmetry is forced. jekyll-feed is in the Gemfile's :jekyll_plugins
  group, so bundler loads it whether or not it is listed in _config.yml, and it
  generates its own /feed.xml -- one feed holding both languages -- unless it
  finds a file already claiming that path. It looks for the source path
  `feed.xml`, not the output URL, so a page under _pages/ does not stop it.
  /it/feed.xml is not a path jekyll-feed knows, so the Italian twin is free to
  live in _pages/it/ with the rest of the Italian pages.

  Nothing may be emitted before the XML declaration, hence the stripping tags.
{%- endcomment -%}
